# showcase-pool-off.env -- ONE BLOCK THAT TURNS EVERY NEW FLEET PIECE OFF FOR THE SHOWCASE (trunk merge, 2026-11-16)
#
# For the showcase's control session, at the trunk's first release: put these lines where the bot process reads its
# environment (the unit `mcshow@.service` reads /srv/showcase/harness/env/<bot>.env). Then take one piece's lines out at
# a time, each with its own read. The inventory behind it is SHOWCASE-NEW.md in this folder; row numbers below are its.
# Made against the trunk at a37c6b6d0 (bots/ is unchanged up to 5753dc748). Format: plain NAME=value, comments on their
# own lines only (a systemd EnvironmentFile takes no comment after a value).
#
# WHAT IS IN IT: 48 lines. The 41 switches the showcase never had that are on by default with a caller on the branch,
# six more whose names are built from a template (STN_<PART> x5, GKF_CLOCK), and PAUSE_RECOVERY_MS (an old name whose
# default the fleet changed). NOT in it, on purpose: the five already off by pool (BUILDRETRY, VISIT_WAIVER,
# UNSITEDWAIT, IDLEWORK_WELL, CRAFTSPARE), ROLES (off unless set `on`), and the eleven that do nothing on the branch
# (BUILDNEXT, BUILDNEXT_BREAKER, CANOPY, STARVE, PLANKEEP, LOOPYIELD, STUCKCLOSE, STUCKFLEET, STUCKFLEET2, STUCKFLEET3,
# TIDYDEAD; also GKF_DEAD, GKF_LEVEL, GKF_CREW).
#
# THE OFF VALUES ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. Each line's comment names the reader (file:line on the branch) and what it
# accepts. Thirteen readers take ONLY the value written here: `0` for IDLEWORK, IDLEWORK_BAGSTOP, IDLEWORK_RETURNFIRST,
# DEPOSITOFFER, DEPOSITRUNG, REPEATWORK, GATHERMEM, PICKSWINGS, IRONCHAIN_TUNNEL, DIRTRUNG_EARTH (`off` leaves them ON),
# and `off` for CHESTMERGE, FULLPLACE, COBBLEROOM (`0` leaves them ON). SANDRUNG is the other way round: `1` is the
# showcase's behaviour. Checked by running, with the wrong value on purpose: `=off` left 8 of those ten ON (the two in
# milestones.mjs were read, not run); `=0` left CHESTMERGE, FULLPLACE and COBBLEROOM ON; `COBBLEROOM=OFF` in capitals
# stayed ON; `SANDRUNG=on` did not bring the rung back; `VILLAGEUNLOCK=no` and `VETOREMEDY=OFF` stayed ON.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS BLOCK DOES NOT COVER -- still different from today's showcase with every line applied
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. leasegen-01 (no switch). Once an hour, at a lease take, superseded lease files are deleted from the pool's state
#    folder (each lease's newest 3 and anything under 4 h are kept); two per-connection timers are cleared on
#    disconnect. A pool-default switch would take one guard at the one call, buildproj.mjs:521 `leaseSweep(dir, now)`.
#    The timers (index.mjs:297, :1192) are a leak fix and need none.
# 2. bagdiet-01 (no switch). A craft tries the three nearest tables before placing its own; monument, wall and
#    tree-farm visits hold at most 64 of an item and bank the rest back; a dug table's drop is looked for farther and
#    once more. A switch would take one reader and a test at six places in skills.mjs: the table candidates (about
#    :6047 and :6073), `PROJECT_VISIT_HOLD` handed to needFromTown (:26287, :31150), `bankBackDue` (:26365, :26935),
#    and the retake's radius and late look (about :7398, :7485).
# 3. idlework-02's hint on the ladder's IRON rung (no switch; found while writing this block, not in SHOWCASE-NEW.md).
#    milestones.mjs:643: at y <= 18 the rung's hint is a depth-aware `mine` target, whatever IDLEWORK says. A switch is
#    one condition on that line (`idleWorkOn() &&`), as the idle rung's own hint already has at :876.
# 4. The idle rung stays in the ladder with IDLEWORK=0, as a rung that is always met (see the chain in the proof below:
#    `idle_work` is listed in both runs). The lap is the showcase's again (patrol decides), but the chain is one entry
#    longer and the controller writes rung-tracking rows (dirtrung-01's `track`), which have no switch.
# 5. New telemetry rows at spawn, no switch: `escdead_mode`, `seapocket_mode`, `bamboowalk_mode`, `visitswitch_mode`,
#    `poolswitch_mode`, the village-unlock mode row, the deposit-offer tallies. Whether the showcase's replay gate and
#    tripwire readers accept row kinds they have never seen was NOT determined.
# 6. Fleet rewrites that stay in the path when their switch is off. Each says in its own comment that off is "the base
#    exactly"; I read them and did not prove them equal by running: poolescape.mjs `poolToolOk` and exit-contract.mjs
#    (now through toolfor.mjs `usablePickaxes` / `HARD_STOP`, under ESCDEAD=0); admission.mjs's deposit decision (now
#    through `depositRunnable` / depositoffer.mjs `depositVerdict`, under DEPOSITOFFER=0 and DEPOSITRUNG=0);
#    oretunnel.mjs `tunnelTargets` (under IRONCHAIN_TUNNEL=0); toolhygiene.mjs `redundantCraft` (under TOOLRANK=off);
#    protectzone.mjs `blocked` / `blockedIn` with their new `deep` argument (null under ESCDEAD=0).
# 7. The llama-server client in llm.mjs (no switch). Inert for the showcase as it is set today: one endpoint, written
#    without the `oai+` prefix (read on the host 11-16 23:13Z). It becomes live the day an endpoint is written `oai+...`.
# 8. THE 33 PROTECTED DECLARATIONS WHERE THE FLEET'S VERSION STANDS (ledgers/review-worklist.json, key `fleet`). Both
#    lines had changed each one; the first pass kept the fleet's text, and whatever the showcase had changed inside is
#    gone unless one of the later fix commits put it back. No switch reaches these. I did not read them.
#      admission.mjs    AdmissionControl
#      airpocket.mjs    airPocketStep, airPocketRow
#      cognitive.mjs    CognitiveLoop
#      deepmine.mjs     slotsOf, DEEPMINE, returnWhy, deepModeDetail
#      escapeguard.mjs  ROW_EVERY_MS, ORDINARY, guardOf, escapeDigDecision
#      index.mjs        connect
#      oretunnel.mjs    tunnelKindsFor
#      protectzone.mjs  blocked, blockedIn, zoneDecision, attachProtectZone
#      reflex.mjs       startReflexes, floodBranch, guardBranch, pillarOut, digStraightUp
#      skills.mjs       tunnelToOre, gather, gatherRun, escapeRecordSnapshot, escapeRecordAt, mine, stairDescend,
#                       stairAscend, deepClose, deepMine
# 9. Showcase code the merge changed or dropped: 688 removed lines between the showcase sha and the branch (skills 341,
#    cognitive 80, reflex 55). Not read.
# 10. Anything in the roughly 4,000 added lines I read only by hunk heads, and any default held in a constant rather
#    than an env name. And bagfix-01show (0e33aa99, live on the showcase since 11-16 23:03Z) is not in this branch at
#    all: it reads `CHESTCARRY` too, so the CHESTCARRY line below must be looked at again when that release is merged.
# 11. GKLEASE2 is the one line with no callable reader (a private constant in skills.mjs). Its value was verified by
#    reading only.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROOF BY RUNNING (2026-11-16)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A throwaway script (kept outside the repo) imported the branch's own modules from a copy of `bots/src` at a37c6b6d0
# and called each switch's own exported reader, in two fresh node processes: both with MEMORY_POOL=showcase and
# LLM_DECISION_COOLDOWN_MS=30000 (as the showcase env has them), one with nothing else, one with this file's 48 lines
# exported. A fresh process each time matters: TOOLRANK, CHESTMERGE, FULLPLACE, COBBLEROOM, ESCDEAD, PICKSWINGS,
# IRONCHAIN_TUNNEL and the two config numbers are read once at module load. The last column asks the reader with ONLY
# that one name set (unset > set), so a line is not credited with a flip its parent made (GKF_*, STN_*, DEPOSITOFFER).
# Nothing was connected to a server; no bot ran.
#
#   RESULT: 47 of 48 lines flip between the two runs; 43 of them also flip alone; 4 are constants with no env argument
#   (shown by the two runs only); 1 has no callable reader (GKLEASE2, verified by reading). 0 lines failed to flip.
#
#   NAME                          value   no block        with block      this name alone (unset>set)
#   IDLEWORK                      0       on              off             on>off
#   IDLEWORK_BAGSTOP              0       on              off             on>off
#   IDLEWORK_RETURNFIRST          0       on              off             on>off
#   LLM_DECISION_COOLDOWN_CAP_MS  0       cooldown=15000  cooldown=30000  cooldown=15000>cooldown=30000
#   PAUSE_RECOVERY_MS             120000  pause=30000     pause=120000    pause=30000>pause=120000
#   ESCDEAD                       0       on              off             on>off
#   SWIMUNDER                     0       on              off             on>off
#   SWIMCENTRE                    0       on              off             on>off
#   DROPANDDIG                    0       on              off             on>off
#   ESCPOCKET                     0       on              off             on>off
#   VILLAGEUNLOCK                 0       on              off             on>off
#   WORKBOARD                     off     on              off             on>off
#   GKFOREVER                     0       on              off             on>off
#   GKF_IDLE                      0       on              off             on>off
#   GKF_CLOCK                     0       on              off             on>off
#   VETOREMEDY                    0       on              off             on>off
#   DEPOSITOFFER                  0       on              off             on>off
#   DEPOSITRUNG                   0       on              off             on>off
#   REPEATWORK                    0       on              off             on>off
#   GATHERMEM                     0       on              off             on>off
#   LOGGATE                       off     on              off             on>off
#   LOGCAP                        off     on              off             on>off
#   LOGCAP_PROMPT                 off     on              off             on>off
#   PICKSWINGS                    0       on              off             on>off
#   TOOLRANK                      off     on              off             const
#   STATIONS                      0       on              off             on>off
#   STN_RETAKE                    0       on              off             on>off
#   STN_SWEEP                     0       on              off             on>off
#   STN_REUSE                     0       on              off             on>off
#   STN_WITHDRAW                  0       on              off             on>off
#   STN_SURPLUS                   0       on              off             on>off
#   STATIONSBACK                  0       on              off             on>off
#   GKLEASE2                      0       no_reader       no_reader       no_reader
#   STAIRUSE                      off     on              off             on>off
#   SHAFTTRAP                     off     on              off             on>off
#   CHESTMERGE                    off     on              off             const
#   FULLPLACE                     off     on              off             const
#   CHESTCARRY                    off     on              off             on>off
#   COBBLEROOM                    off     on              off             const
#   LIDGROUND                     off     on              off             on>off
#   SANDRUNG                      1       rung_out        rung_in         rung_out>rung_in
#   MONUSTUCK                     off     on              off             on>off
#   STUCKCELLS                    off     on              off             on>off
#   BAMBOOWALK                    0       on              off             on>off
#   IRONCHAIN_TUNNEL              0       on              off             on>off
#   BUILDWAIT                     0       on              off             on>off
#   DIRTRUNG_EARTH                0       on              off             on>off
#   GKSTAY                        0       on              off             on>off
#
# THE LADDER AND THE SPAWN ROWS. The same two runs, through the controller the bot builds its chain with
# (`new MilestoneController(bot, 'gatherer').chain`) and the pure detail functions features.mjs writes at spawn. The
# third line of each group is the SHOWCASE SHA'S OWN SOURCE (6ed264b9) run the same way, where it has the thing.
#   chain, no block:      gather_dirt_16 > gather_oak_log_12 > gather_cobblestone_8 > stockpile_wood > (8 craft and iron
#                         rungs) > stockpile_stone > idle_work > patrol > return > deposit_surplus
#   chain, with block:    gather_dirt_16 > gather_oak_log_12 > gather_sand_8 > gather_cobblestone_8 > stockpile_wood >
#                         (the same 8) > stockpile_stone > idle_work > patrol > deposit_surplus > return
#   chain, showcase sha:  gather_dirt_16 > gather_oak_log_12 > gather_sand_8 > gather_cobblestone_8 > stockpile_wood >
#                         (the same 8) > stockpile_stone > patrol > deposit_surplus > return
#     -> with the block the chain is the showcase's but for ONE entry, `idle_work` (item 4 above: always met when off).
#   town deposit's kept targets:  no block {"dirt":16}   with block {"dirt":16,"sand":8}   showcase sha {"dirt":16,"sand":8}
#   config:                       no block cooldown=15000 pause=30000   with block cooldown=30000 pause=120000
#                                 showcase sha cooldown=30000 pause=120000
#   idle rotation:        no block grounds,iron,grounds,logs,grounds,coal,grounds,scout
#                         with block iron,logs,iron,coal,logs,iron,coal,scout   (unused: the idle rung is off)
#   escdead_mode:         no block `on=1 pin_min=30 wide=r8/d4 ...`      with block `on=0 pin_min=30 wide=r8/d4 ...`
#   escpocket_mode:       no block `on=1 dig=wide_tier reach=4.5 ...`    with block `on=0 dig=wide_tier reach=4.5 ...`
#   lid clear mode:       no block `... budget_max=15000 ground=1`       with block `... budget_max=15000 ground=0`
#   villageunlock mode:   no block `on=1 max_cells=12 stuck_min=20 ...`  with block `on=0 max_cells=12 stuck_min=20 ...`
#   CONTROL (must NOT move, and does not): the five pool defaults read the same in both runs --
#     visitswitch_mode `buildretry=0 (pool) visit_waiver=0 (pool) pool=showcase`
#     poolswitch_mode  `unsitedwait=0 (pool) idlework_well=0 (pool) craftspare=0 (pool) pool=showcase`
# What the run does NOT show: that a switch being off makes the bot behave as the showcase sha does. It shows that each
# reader answers off. Whether the code behind an off switch is the showcase's exactly is item 6 above.
#
# =====================================================================================================================
# THE BLOCK
# =====================================================================================================================

# --- idlework-01, idlework-02 (row 1): off = the lap is `patrol` again (walk 80 blocks out and back), no work batches.
# idlework.mjs:28  `String(env?.IDLEWORK ?? '1').trim() !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0` is off
IDLEWORK=0
# idlework.mjs:88  `String(env?.IDLEWORK_BAGSTOP ?? '1').trim() !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0`. Moot under IDLEWORK=0; kept so
# that taking IDLEWORK out later does not also bring the bag stop in unasked.
IDLEWORK_BAGSTOP=0
# milestones.mjs:1011  `!/^\s*0\s*$/.test(...)`  -- ONLY `0`. Off = the sustaining lap's old order (deposit_surplus
# before return) and the old "met" rule of deposit_surplus. Independent of IDLEWORK.
IDLEWORK_RETURNFIRST=0

# --- cooldown15-01 (row 2): the showcase sha reads `Number(req('LLM_DECISION_COOLDOWN_MS', '20000'))`, no cap, and its
# env sets 30000. config.mjs:63-68 `cappedCooldownMs`: a cap that is not a positive finite number is IGNORED and the env
# value passes through (line 66), so 0 reproduces the showcase sha for ANY env value. 30000 gives the same number only
# while the env value stays at or under 30000 (it is the fleet's documented rollback). Read at config.mjs:303-304.
LLM_DECISION_COOLDOWN_CAP_MS=0

# --- pause30-01 (row 11): the showcase sha reads `Number(req('PAUSE_RECOVERY_MS', '120000'))` and its env does not set
# the name, so it pauses 120 s. config.mjs:80 `resolvePauseRecoveryMs` (read at :217): unset is now 30000; a positive
# number passes through. 120000 is the showcase sha's value.
PAUSE_RECOVERY_MS=120000

# --- escdead-01 (row 3): off = no wide swim, no flood-in breach, no pinned last swing, the zone guard's floor_y rule.
# toolfor.mjs:74-75  `!/^(0|off|false|no)$/i.test(String(env?.ESCDEAD ?? '1').trim())`
ESCDEAD=0

# --- swimunder-01, swimcentre-01, dropanddig-01, escpocket-01 with seapocket-01 (row 4): off = the drowning rescue as
# the showcase has it. All four readers: `!/^(0|off|false|no)$/i.test(String(env?.NAME ?? '1').trim())`.
# swimunder.mjs:27-28
SWIMUNDER=0
# swimcentre.mjs:32-33
SWIMCENTRE=0
# dropdig.mjs:37-38
DROPANDDIG=0
# escdead.mjs:189-190 (also the long-breath tier and the trap-pocket pricing in index.mjs)
ESCPOCKET=0

# --- villageunlock-01 (row 5): off = no bot toggles a trapdoor or fence gate at a village; the build order never asks.
# villageunlock.mjs:65-67  lower-cased, `v === '0' || v === 'off' || v === 'false'` (no trim; `no` is NOT off)
VILLAGEUNLOCK=0

# --- workboard-01 (row 6): off = the order chain as before, the model is asked on a grounds lap as on any other.
# townwork.mjs:26-28  trimmed, lower-cased, one of off|0|false|no (`shadow` computes and logs, issues nothing)
WORKBOARD=off

# --- gkforever-01 (row 7): off = no grounds lap in the idle rotation, the tidy's ring as groundskeeper-01 has it.
# gkforever.mjs:47-51 and idlework.mjs:58-59: trimmed, lower-cased, one of 0|off|false|no. GKFOREVER=0 alone turns
# every part off; the two part lines are kept so the parts can be let in one at a time.
GKFOREVER=0
# idlework.mjs:59 (the rotation) and gkforever.mjs:51 (`GKF_<PART>`)
GKF_IDLE=0
# gkforever.mjs:51 (`GKF_<PART>`, a template: the name does not appear literally in the source)
GKF_CLOCK=0

# --- vetoremedy-01 (row 8): off = a veto is followed by the cooldown and the model, never by a fixed remedy.
# vetoremedy.mjs:46 and :52  EXACT string, no trim, no lower-casing: `v === '0' || v === 'false' || v === 'off'`
VETOREMEDY=0

# --- depositoffer-01, decbundle-01 (row 8): off = `deposit` is always among the model's choices; the deposit rung has
# its old 12-item floor.
# depositoffer.mjs:29  `String(env.DEPOSITOFFER ?? '1') !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0`, no trim
DEPOSITOFFER=0
# depositoffer.mjs:26  `String(env?.DEPOSITRUNG ?? '1') !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0`, no trim (it turns the offer off too)
DEPOSITRUNG=0

# --- repeatwork-01 (row 8): off = the repeat window refuses a fourth identical key whatever its last run gained.
# repeatwork.mjs:26  `String(env.REPEATWORK ?? '1') !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0`, no trim
REPEATWORK=0

# --- gathermem-01 (row 8): off = no memory of failed gather targets or areas, no refusal and no prompt line from it.
# gathermem.mjs:24  `String(env?.GATHERMEM ?? '1').trim() !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0`
GATHERMEM=0

# --- loggate-01, logcap-02 (row 8): off = gathering logs is never refused for the town's stock, no TOWN WOOD line.
# All three: logcap.mjs:41 `['0', 'off', 'false', 'no']`, trimmed and lower-cased.
# logcap.mjs:132
LOGGATE=off
# logcap.mjs:46
LOGCAP=off
# logcap.mjs:109
LOGCAP_PROMPT=off

# --- ironchain-02 (row 8): off = an iron pickaxe craft is admitted as asked, never rewritten to stone.
# pickswings.mjs:22  `String(env?.PICKSWINGS ?? '1').trim() !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0`
PICKSWINGS=0

# --- toolrank-01 (row 8): off = tool hygiene's rule as the showcase has it (pickaxes only, no pair rule).
# toolhygiene.mjs:41-42  `/^(0|off|false|no)$/i` on the trimmed value; read ONCE at module load
TOOLRANK=off

# --- stations-01 (row 9): off = no furnace retake, no sweep of stray stations, no reuse of town stations, no withdraw
# before a craft, no table burned as fuel. stations.mjs:40-46: trimmed, lower-cased, one of 0|off|false|no.
# STATIONS=0 alone turns every part off; the five part lines (`STN_<PART>`, a template at :46) are kept so the parts
# can be let in one at a time.
STATIONS=0
STN_RETAKE=0
STN_SWEEP=0
STN_REUSE=0
STN_WITHDRAW=0
STN_SURPLUS=0

# --- stationsback-01 (row 9): off = a retake does not chase its drop or retry an aborted dig.
# stationsback.mjs:25 and :27  `/^(0|off|false|no)$/i` on the trimmed value
STATIONSBACK=0

# --- gklease-02 (row 9): off = the sweep's give-ups are per bot (gklease-01), not shared by the town.
# skills.mjs:29037  `!['0', 'off', 'false', 'no'].includes(String(process.env.GKLEASE2 ?? '1').trim().toLowerCase())`
# A private constant: NO CALLABLE READER. Verified by reading only.
GKLEASE2=0

# --- stairuse-01, shafttrap-02 (row 10): off = the town stair is used as the showcase uses it; no stair exit hand-over
# from the reflex. Both: trimmed, lower-cased, one of off|0|false|no.
# shaftgeom.mjs:888
STAIRUSE=off
# shaftgeom.mjs:835
SHAFTTRAP=off

# --- chestmerge-01 (row 12): off = a full town chest is not merged inside; the deposit banks into empty slots only.
# chestmerge.mjs:33  trimmed, lower-cased, `!== 'off'`  -- ONLY `off`; read ONCE at module load
CHESTMERGE=off

# --- fullplace-01 (row 12): off = a full-chest deposit ends with its refusal and advice, as before.
# fullplace.mjs:17  trimmed, lower-cased, `!== 'off'`  -- ONLY `off`; read ONCE at module load
FULLPLACE=off

# --- chestcarry-01 (row 12): off = one chest budget for every bot, carried chest or not.
# chestfull.mjs:45 and :47  `/^(0|off|false|no)$/i` on the trimmed value. LOOK AGAIN when bagfix-01show is merged:
# that showcase release reads the same name.
CHESTCARRY=off

# --- cobbleroom-01 (row 12): off = the junk well takes surplus cobble only at the proven cap (cobblekeep-01).
# cobblecap.mjs:245  `(process.env.COBBLEROOM ?? 'on') !== 'off'`  -- ONLY the exact string `off` (no trim, no
# lower-casing); read ONCE at module load
COBBLEROOM=off

# --- lidground-01 (row 12): off = only wood (and cobble) comes off a chest lid; natural ground is refused as before.
# lidrule.mjs:102  `/^(off|0|false|no)$/i` on the trimmed value
LIDGROUND=off

# --- sandrung-01 (row 13): the showcase HAS the sand rung, the fleet retired it. 1 = the rung back in its place
# (between wood and cobblestone) and the 8 sand the town deposit keeps for it.
# sandrung.mjs:19  `String(env?.SANDRUNG ?? '0').trim() === '1'`  -- ONLY `1` restores it (`on` does not)
SANDRUNG=1

# --- monustuck-01 (row 14): off = a build visit bans no stand and never ends a cell `no_stand` for bans.
# stuckcells.mjs:58  trimmed, lower-cased, one of off|0|false|no
MONUSTUCK=off

# --- stuckcells-01, the part outside the waiver (row 14): off = no support chain for a stair cell with nothing to
# click against. Two readers with the same expression: stuckcells.mjs:36 (exported) and shaftvisit.mjs:22 (a private
# copy, verified by reading): trimmed, lower-cased, one of off|0|false|no
STUCKCELLS=off

# --- bamboowalk-01 (row 15): off = the plugin installs nothing; bamboo collides where minecraft-data bakes it.
# bamboowalk.mjs:28  trimmed, lower-cased, one of 0|off|false|no
BAMBOOWALK=0

# --- ironchain-01 (row 16): off = the ore tunnel picks its target with its own filter only (hazard and home radius).
# ironchain.mjs:10  `String(env?.IRONCHAIN_TUNNEL ?? '1').trim() !== '0'`  -- ONLY `0`; the constant at :11 is read
